# .specs/project/.env.test: THIS project's test values. SECRET: ignored by git, never commit, never paste into a document.
# Same names the project's TEST-ENVIRONMENT.md mentions as $NAME. The first file that defines a name wins:
#   this file > ~/.loop-harness/.env (your machine, every project) > plugin/shared/.env. A real environment variable wins over all.
# The harness appends, below, the TEST names this file does not define yet (copied from ~/.loop-harness/.env and plugin/shared/.env; LOCAL_URL
# defaults to the local panel). It never overwrites a line you wrote.
# Only DEV and localhost values. Quote a value with # & % { } ? ^ using single quotes. Lists use `;` (write \; for a literal ;).

# Test users: lists aligned by position. Leave them out to use the generic account of ~/.loop-harness/.env.
# TEST_USER_EMAILS=first@company.com;second@company.com
# TEST_USER_PASSWORDS=
# TEST_USER_ROLES=customer;admin

# LOCAL_URL=https://localhost:5001
# ROUTE_PREFIX=/api/v1
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
